# Description: 
> The following program implements a secure blockchain for chain of custody forms.
> This blockchain implements the following features:

1. init: 
This function determines if the blockchain file is present. If not, it creates a genesis block and initializes the blockchain. If the file exists, it verifies its presence.   

2. add -c case_id -i item_id [-i item_id...] -g creator -p password:  
Adds an evidence item, or a list of items, to a case. Requires the name of the creator and their password to add successfully.  

3. checkout -i item_id -p password:
After verifying the owner's password, it checks out an item for investigation and adds a CHECKEDOUT block.  

4. checkin -i item_id -p password
After verifying the owner's password, it checks the item back into custody and adds a CHECKEDIN block.

5. remove -i item_id -y reason -p password
After verifying the owner's password and providing a reason for removal, it ensures the selected item is CHECKEDIN and removes it from the chain, adding a REMOVED block.   

6. show cases
If authorized it lists all case IDs, case IDs encrypted if not authorized.

7. show items -c case_id
List all the item IDs in a selected case

8. show history [-c case_id] [-i item_id] [-n num_entries] [-r] -p password
Shows the activity history of a given case with additional filter options for a certain item ID and/or number of entries. Output is encrypted unless authorized access. 

9. summary -c item_id
Shows the total number of CHECKEDIN, CHECKEDOUT, and removed items in a case.

10. verify
Validates the blockchain by checking for the following: Genesis block, duplicate previous hashes, sequential linking, bad blocks and messages, and actions after removal



